{
  "_comment": "The shared case table: tests/supabase_cases.py turns each case into SQL for the throwaway Postgres of tests/test_supabase_sql.py, and tests/fake_supabase.py reads the same file, so the fake and the SQL give the same answers. '_format' says what each field means.",
  "_format": [
    "Each case is one call. 'as' is the caller: 'b', 'c' or 'd' (a user's session, role authenticated; a personal worker holds its user's session) or 'anon'.",
    "Every case starts from these rows. Users c and d are approved; user b is not. Machine mc is c's, with the live personal worker wc (no local keys); machine md is d's, with the live personal worker wd. Settings are the defaults (Free: plan_file_limit 50 MiB).",
    "Every case has one job, 'the job' (<job> in names), on a machine: job.machine ('mc' or 'md'; default the caller's machine, else 'mc'). Its user is the machine's owner. job: status (default 'ready'; 'deleting' also sets deleted_at), input_kind (default 'video').",
    "state.settings and state.access set columns (access of the caller, or of c for 'anon'). state.own_worker: absent, wc and wd are live; null, both are stopped. state.rate: a number, this hour's request count of the job's user (private.rate). state.requests: rows of the job, oldest first: route, state (default 'pending'), sealed {worker, agent} (a job_secrets row sealed to that worker). state.objects: Storage objects [{bucket, name, size, age}], age in seconds (default 0: made now).",
    "args by fn: relay {route, query, body, text, sealed}, where sealed 'valid' is a well-formed key sealed to the newest live worker of the job's machine (private.live_worker; a random id when it is offline) and {worker, agent} names the worker ('wc', 'wd'; default that live worker) and the agent (default 'opus'); delete_job (the job); own_claim_request {worker, kinds}; own_worker_start {machine, local_keys}; own_publish {worker, view, live, snapshots, row}; own_files {worker, put [{path, bytes, object (default <user>/<job>/<sha256[:16]>/<path>), sha256 (default 0123456789abcdef and 48 zeros), role (default 'result'), content_type}], drop}; own_logs {worker, rows}; own_job_create {worker, name, kind, bytes}; job_objects {limit (default 1000)} (the job's objects); own_orphans {worker, limit (default 1000)}; storage_insert {bucket, name, size}, an upload under the Storage policies; storage_delete {bucket, name}, a delete under the policies.",
    "In names, and in the strings of an expected answer, <b> <c> <d> are the users' ids and <job> is the job's id.",
    "expect: {'error': regex}, matched case-insensitively against the message. Errors from a table constraint match 'check constraint', and refused table or function grants match 'permission denied'. Or {'ok': value}: 'uuid' for any uuid; a list for set-returning functions, same length and in the same order, each row containing the listed fields (rows of own_claim_request as JSON; job_objects rows {name, created_at} and own_orphans rows {name}, oldest first); an object that the answer contains, where relay's extra key 'withdrawn' is the number of the job's withdrawn requests after the call; null for void functions (the call succeeds); a number for storage_delete (objects deleted); else equal. A case runs in its own transaction, which is rolled back."
  ],
  "cases": [
